  - Ed25519
  - negative-first testing
  - research software
abstract: >
  Equal3 is research code (release decision NO-GO, not for production) that studies how a single
  host could prove that its local state was not rolled back. It combines a bounded delta codec, an
  SQLite state store with version compare-and-swap and HMAC-chained receipts, and a trust domain
  of anchor service, attested writer, root-authorised key rotation, signed epoch and commit
  witnesses with request-lineage binding. Every audit round reports that a joint rollback of all
  local components is not detected. Version 0.7.22-research is the state of 2026-10-25; the
  repository adds documentation and a provenance check, and keeps all imported files unchanged.
